---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
import ScreenshotFigure from "../components/ScreenshotFigure.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Meeting Pulse features | Private status for macOS"
  description="See how Meeting Pulse detects supported meetings, shares a private viewer, handles manual status, and stays honest about unavailable states."
  canonicalPath="/features/"
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Features"
    title="One signal, with enough context to trust it."
    description="Meeting Pulse keeps the owner’s controls on the Mac and gives viewers the small answer they came for."
  >
    <div class="button-row" style="margin-top: var(--space-lg)">
      <a class="button button--accent" href="/download/">Download for macOS</a>
      <a class="button" href="/privacy/">Read privacy</a>
    </div>
  </PageIntro>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="split-section">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">01 · Detection</p>
        <h2>Automatic when it can be. Clear when it cannot.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split-section__body">
        <ScreenshotFigure
          light="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-diagnostics-window-light.jpg"
          dark="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-diagnostics-window-dark.jpg"
          alt="Meeting Pulse diagnostics window showing detection health"
          caption="Diagnostics stay with the owner, where they can be acted on."
        />
        <p>
          The owner app uses macOS Accessibility APIs to detect Google Meet in
          Chrome and native Slack Huddles. It does not need a browser extension,
          Slack bot, OAuth, calendar access, or Screen Recording.
        </p>
        <div class="callout">
          <strong>Detection is not a promise to guess.</strong>
          <p>
            If a permission is missing or a state is uncertain, the product
            keeps that uncertainty visible.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="split-section">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">02 · Controls</p>
        <h2>Automatic status plus a human override.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split-section__body">
        <ScreenshotFigure
          light="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-station-watch-call-okay-light.jpg"
          dark="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-station-watch-call-okay-dark.jpg"
          alt="Meeting Pulse Station showing manual status and call okay controls"
          caption="Station keeps manual controls and call okay close to the owner."
        />
        <p>
          Set Busy or Available for a duration when the owner knows more than
          the detector can. A separate Call okay signal lets someone tell the
          viewer that a call can still come through.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="split-section">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">03 · Private viewer</p>
        <h2>A link for the person checking in.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split-section__body">
        <ScreenshotFigure
          light="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-viewer-pairing-light.jpg"
          dark="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-viewer-pairing-dark.jpg"
          alt="Meeting Pulse viewer pairing screen"
          caption="Pair a browser viewer from Station."
          width={1280}
          height={577}
        />
        <p>
          The viewer opens on a phone or laptop. It shows the availability
          state, optional owner name, and call-okay copy. It does not expose
          meeting titles, URLs, participants, or meeting content.
        </p>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="/docs/pairing/">Read pairing docs</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">04 · Trust states</p>
      <h2>Unavailable is part of the feature set.</h2>
      <p>
        Offline, revoked, malformed, and stale states have their own language.
        The viewer does not quietly turn a missing signal into permission to
        interrupt.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="card-kicker">Stale</span>
        <h3>Say when the signal is old.</h3>
        <p>Viewers can tell the difference between a current state and a status that needs attention.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="card-kicker">Offline</span>
        <h3>Keep “not connected” visible.</h3>
        <p>Network or pairing problems get a direct message and a next step.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="card-kicker">Revoked</span>
        <h3>Give the owner control of access.</h3>
        <p>Viewer links can be managed from Station rather than living forever by accident.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
